description:
CSP configuration in index.html is too permissive and allows unsafe inline scripts.

## File
- index.html (line 24)

## Current (Insecure)
```
script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
connect-src 'self' blob: http://localhost:* http://127.0.0.1:* https://*;
```

## Issues
1. **unsafe-inline in script-src** - Allows XSS via injected inline scripts
2. **unsafe-inline in style-src** - Enables CSS injection attacks
3. **https://* in connect-src** - Allows connections to ANY HTTPS server (data exfiltration)
4. **Missing directives** - No frame-ancestors, base-uri, form-action

## Recommended Fix
```
script-src 'self';
style-src 'self' 'nonce-{random}';
connect-src 'self' blob: http://localhost:* http://127.0.0.1:*;
frame-ancestors 'none';
base-uri 'self';
form-action 'self';
```

## Priority
CRITICAL - Enables XSS and data exfiltration

Sync server defaults to allowing ANY origin if CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS not set.

## File
- server/src/main.rs (lines 50-53)

## Current Behaviour
```rust
} else {
    tracing::warn!("CORS: Allowing any origin...");
    cors = cors.allow_origin(Any);
}
```

## Issue
- Default allows cross-origin requests from ANY domain
- Enables CSRF attacks if SPA hosted on different domain
- Warning logged but server still runs insecurely

## Fix Required
Default to REFUSING rather than ALLOWING:
```rust
let allowed_origins = std::env::var("CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS")
    .expect("CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS must be set in production");
```

Or at minimum, only allow same-origin by default.

## Priority
CRITICAL - Enables CSRF attacks

Add sr-only (screen-reader-only) text to provide context for screen reader users.

## Areas Needing sr-only Text
1. **Current page indicators** - Which note is selected
2. **Loading states** - When content is loading
3. **Action results** - Confirmation of completed actions
4. **Icon button context** - Additional context for icon buttons
5. **Form field requirements** - Password requirements, validation rules

## Implementation
Add Tailwind sr-only class or equivalent:
```css
.sr-only {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  padding: 0;
  margin: -1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
  white-space: nowrap;
  border: 0;
}
```

## Examples
```svelte
<button>
  <Icon name="delete" />
  <span class="sr-only">Delete note: {noteTitle}</span>
</button>
```

## Priority
Medium - Improves screen reader experience
